# Arbor versioning

**Product milestones** (Version 1, 2, 3 in `PROJECT.md`) describe eras of capability. **Package/git tags** (`v2.0.0`, `v2.1.0`, `v3.0.0`) track shipped releases.

## Rules

1. **`v2.0.0` = Version 2 complete** — automation and discoverability (jobs, FTS, watch, OCR, Word). The old single-column UI. Do not re-open v2 scope.

2. **Version 3 shipped as `v3.0.0`.** Work toward Version 3 shipped as **`v2.1.0`, `v2.2.0`, `v2.3.0`, `v2.4.0`, `v2.5.0`**. Package `v2.1.0` was the first step after Version 2.

3. **`v3.0.0` is the Version 3 completion package** — the features listed under Version 3 in `PROJECT.md` (shell, flashcards, quiz, concepts, diagrams, citations, cross-document linking, knowledge graph, embeddings, semantic search) and the 2026-10-17 Linux live run on the [implementation checklist](docs/implementation-checklist.md). Mac proof does not block the tag. The git tag is cut when the release lands. Two Notes constructs (tables, emphasis) were not in any live digest.

4. **Version 4 shipped as `v4.0.0`.** Work toward Version 4 shipped as **`v3.1.0`, `v3.2.0`, `v3.3.0`, `v3.4.0`, `v3.5.0`**. The 2026-10-18 Linux live run closed it. Issue #20 stays open until the parent closes it after `v4.0.0`. **Version 5 is in progress.** It ships as **`v4.1.0`, `v4.2.0`, …** until `v5.0.0`.

5. **CHANGELOG and package versions stay aligned** across worker, desktop, and Tauri (`python/src/arbor_worker/__init__.py`, `pyproject.toml`, `desktop/package.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `tauri.conf.json`). `arbor-worker --version` reads `__init__.py`.

6. **Version gates** live in [`docs/implementation-checklist.md`](docs/implementation-checklist.md). Local/VM tests gate every merge. A Linux live run gates the product-version tags (`v3.0.0`, `v4.0.0`, …). Mac batches are optional and never block a tag. Do not live-test every small feature. Do not start the next product version until the current version’s Linux live run is recorded.

